{"seq":60,"at":"2026-10-23","kind":"reworded","target":{"type":"wording","id":"w12289"},"reason":"The card's 'world's first industrial nation to decide to stop using nuclear power' is contested: Italy ended its nuclear programme after a 1987 referendum and Germany itself first agreed a phase-out in 2000. Narrowed to the uncontested fact: the 2011 post-Fukushima decision to shut all plants by 2022 (card text kept in cardText).","by":"provenance-research","sources":[{"url":"https://world-nuclear.org/information-library/country-profiles/countries-g-n/italy"},{"url":"https://world-nuclear.org/information-library/country-profiles/countries-g-n/germany"},{"url":"https://www.base.bund.de/DE/themen/kt/ausstieg-atomkraft/ausstieg_node.html"}],"changes":[{"field":"en","old":"Which country, in 2011, became the world's first industrial nation to decide to stop using nuclear power?","new":"Which country decided in 2011, after the Fukushima disaster, to shut down all its nuclear power plants by 2022?"},{"field":"de","old":"Wie heißt das Land, das 2011 als erste Industrienation der Welt beschloss, Atomenergie nicht mehr zu nutzen?","new":"Welches Land beschloss 2011 nach der Katastrophe von Fukushima, alle seine Kernkraftwerke bis 2022 abzuschalten?"},{"field":"ru","old":"Какая страна в 2011 году первой из индустриальных стран мира решила отказаться от использования атомной энергии?","new":"Какая страна в 2011 году после катастрофы на «Фукусиме» решила закрыть все свои атомные электростанции к 2022 году?"},{"field":"cardText","new":"Wie heißt das Land, das 2011 als erste Industrienation der Welt beschloss, Atomenergie nicht mehr zu nutzen?"}],"hash":"17e17d0f5f0c","actor":{"kind":"agent","name":"provenance-research"},"run":"provenance-research-2026-10-23","chain":"74acd6d2bace2ff1fb7d0365d0149b7c043803ab051f12cbf6c8a9c14b54b1fa"},
